\[(x^4 - 4x^3 + 14x^2) - (4x - 13).\]

Now, we can factor out the greatest common factor from each pair:
\[x^2(x^2 - 4x + 14) - 4(x - 3).\]

Next, we can factor out the common factor $(x - 3)$:
\[(x - 3)(x^2 - 4x + 13).\]

Finally, we can factor the quadratic expression $x^2 - 4x + 13$:
\[(x - 3)(x - 1)(x - 13).\]

Therefore, the complete factorization of the given polynomial is:
