Let
\[a_n = \sqrt{1 + \left( 1 + \frac{1}{n} \right)^2} + \sqrt{1 + \left( 1 - \frac{1}{n} \right)^2}.\]Compute
\[\frac{1}{a_1} + \frac{1}{a_2} + \frac{1}{a_3} + \dots + \frac{1}{a_{100}}.\]

Solution:
answer:  We have that
\[a_n = \sqrt{1 + \left( 1 + \frac{1}{n} \right)^2} + \sqrt{1 + \left( 1 - \frac{1}{n} \right)^2} = \sqrt{1 + \frac{1}{n^2}} + \sqrt{1 + \frac{1}{n^2}} = 2.\]
