answer:  Since $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are odd functions, we have $f(-x) = -f(x)$ and $g(-x) = -g(x)$. Therefore, $f(-x)g(-x) = (-f(x))(-g(x)) = f(-x)g(x) = f(x)g(x)$. This means that $f(x)g(x)$ is an even function.

Final Answer: The final answer is "even". I hope it is correct.
