Problem:
Evaluate the product \[(\sqrt 5+\sqrt6+\sqrt7)(-\sqrt 5+\sqrt6+\sqrt7)(\sqrt 5-\sqrt6+\sqrt7)(\sqrt 5+\sqrt6-\sqrt7).\]

Solution:
answer:  We can use the difference of squares formula to simplify the expression. The difference of squares formula states that $(a+b)(a-b) = a^2 - b^2$.

In this case, we have:

\[(\sqrt 5+\sqrt6+\sqrt7)(-\sqrt 5+\sqrt6+\sqrt7)(\sqrt 5-\sqrt6+\sqrt7)(\sqrt 5+\sqrt6-\sqrt7).\]

