Problem:
Find $n$ if $\gcd(n,40) = 10$ and $\mathop{\text{lcm}}[n,40] = 280$.

Solution:
answer:  We know that $\gcd(n,40) \cdot \mathop{\text{lcm}}[n,40] = n \cdot 40$. Substituting the given values, we have:

$$10 \cdot 280 = n \cdot 40$$

$$2800 = n \cdot 40$$

$$n = \frac{2800}{40}$$

$$n = \boxed{70}$$
