\begin{align*}
x &\equiv 5 \pmod{7} \\
x &\equiv 10 \pmod{11} \\
x &\equiv 10 \pmod{13}
\end{align*}

We can solve this system of congruences using the Chinese Remainder Theorem.

The solution is $x \equiv 905 \pmod{1001}$.

Therefore, the largest integer less than $2010$ that satisfies the conditions is $\boxed{905}$.
