\[ 2 \cdot 4 + 2 - 18 = 8 + 2 - 18 = -8 \]

Now, find the remainder when \(-8\) is divided by 19:
\[ -8 \equiv 11 \pmod{19} \]

Therefore, the remainder when \( 2a + b - c \) is divided by 19 is:
\[ \boxed{11} \]
