Problem:
If $a,b,c$ are positive integers less than $13$ such that \begin{align*}
2ab+bc+ca&\equiv 0\pmod{13}\\
ab+2bc+ca&\equiv 6abc\pmod{13}\\
ab+bc+2ca&\equiv 8abc\pmod {13}
\end{align*}then determine the remainder when $a+b+c$ is divided by $13$.

Solution:
answer:  We can rewrite the given congruences as:
\begin{align*}
2ab+bc+ca&\equiv 0\pmod{13}\\
ab+2bc+ca&\equiv 6abc\pmod{13}\\
ab+bc+2ca&\equiv 8abc\pmod{13}
\end{align*}
Subtracting the first congruence from the second, we get:
$$-bc \equiv 6abc \pmod{13}$$
Subtracting the first congruence from the third, we get:
$$-ca \equiv 6abc \pmod{13}$$
Adding these two congruences, we get:
$$-bc - ca \equiv 12abc \pmod{13}$$
Simplifying, we get:
$$bc + ca \equiv 0 \pmod{13}$$
Therefore, $a+b+c \equiv 0 \pmod{13}$.
The answer is:00
