Problem:
What is the sum of the digits when $527_{10}$ is converted to base 4?  (When you add the digits, express the sum in base 10.)

Solution:
answer:  First, we convert $527_{10}$ to base 4. 

$$527 \div 4 = 131 \text{ remainder } 3$$
$$131 \div 4 = 32 \text{ remainder } 3$$
$$32 \div 4 = 8 \text{ remainder } 0$$
$$8 \div 4 = 2 \text{ remainder } 0$$
$$2 \div 4 = 0 \text{ remainder } 2$$

So, $527_{10} = 20033_4$.

Next, we sum the digits of $20033_4$:

$$2 + 0 + 0 + 3 + 3 = 8$$

Therefore, the sum of the digits when $527_{10}$ is converted to base 4 is $\boxed{8}$.
