\[87_{3} = 2210_3\]

This base-3 representation has 4 digits.

Now, we compare the number of digits in the base-2 and base-3 representations:

\[7 - 4 = 3\]

Therefore, the base-10 number 87 has \(\boxed{3}\) more digits when expressed in base 2 than when expressed in base 3.
