4&1&&&&&&&&\\
5&2&&&&&&&&\\
6&7&8&8&&&&&&\\
7&1&1&2&3&3&3&5&6&8\\
8&0&4&4&6&6&6&6&8&\\
9&1&3&5&5&7&&&&\\
\end{tabular}

Solution:
answer:  First, we find the median of the data. The median is the middle value when the data is arranged in ascending order. Arranging the data, we get:

41, 52, 67, 68, 71, 71, 72, 73, 73, 75, 80, 84, 84, 86, 86, 86, 88, 91, 93, 95, 95, 97

The median is 75.

Next, we find the mode of the data. The mode is the value that appears most frequently. In this case, 86 appears 4 times, which is more frequent than any other value.

Now, we calculate the arithmetic mean of the median and the mode:

$$\frac{75 + 86}{2} = \frac{161}{2} = 80.5.$$

