Problem:
Square tiles measuring 4 inches on each side will be used to tile a 1-foot by 1-foot area. How many of these tiles are needed?

Solution:
answer:  First, we need to convert the dimensions of the area from feet to inches, since the tiles are measured in inches. There are 12 inches in a foot, so a 1-foot by 1-foot area is 12 inches by 12 inches.

Next, we calculate the area of the area in square inches:
\[ 12 \text{ inches} \times 12 \text{ inches} = 144 \text{ square inches} \]

Then, we calculate the area of one tile in square inches:
\[ 4 \text{ inches} \times 4 \text{ inches} = 16 \text{ square inches} \]

To find the number of tiles needed, we divide the area of the area by the area of one tile:
\[ \frac{144 \text{ square inches}}{16 \text{ square inches per tile}} = 9 \text{ tiles} \]

Therefore, the number of tiles needed is \(\boxed{9}\).
