Problem:
A $\textit{palindrome}$ is an integer that reads the same forwards and backwards. How many positive 3-digit palindromes are multiples of $3$?

Solution:
answer:  A 3-digit palindrome has the form $aba$$, where $a$ and $b$ are digits. Therefore, $a$ can be any digit from 1 to 9, and $b$ can be any digit from 0 to 9. This gives us a total of $9 \times 10 = 90$ possible 3-digit palindromes.

