Problem:
A regular hexagon is divided into six congruent equilateral triangles. If the perimeter of one of the triangles is 39 inches, what is the perimeter of the regular hexagon, in inches?

Solution:
answer:  Since a regular hexagon is divided into six congruent equilateral triangles, each side of the hexagon is the same as the side of one of the triangles. Given that the perimeter of one of the triangles is 39 inches, we can find the length of one side of the triangle by dividing the perimeter by 3:

\[
\text{Side length of triangle} = \frac{39}{3} = 13 \text{ inches}
\]

Since the hexagon is made up of six such triangles, the perimeter of the hexagon is six times the side length of one triangle:

\[
\text{Perimeter of hexagon} = 6 \times 13 = 78 \text{ inches}
\]

Therefore, the perimeter of the regular hexagon is \boxed{78} inches.
