\[ t = 3 \]

Now that we have \( t = 3 \), we substitute \( t \) into the second equation to find \( y \):
\[ y = 3 - 21 \]
\[ y = -18 \]

Therefore, the value of \( y \) is \(\boxed{-18}\).
