Problem:
Four typists can type a total of 600 memos in three days. At that rate, how many memos can three typists type in one day?

Solution:
answer:  First, let's determine the rate at which one typist can type memos. Since four typists can type 600 memos in three days, one typist can type:

\[
\frac{600\text{ memos}}{4\text{ typists} \times 3\text{ days}} = \frac{600\text{ memos}}{12\text{ days}} = 50\text{ memos per day}
\]

Now, if one typist can type 50 memos per day, then three typists can type:

\[
3\text{ typists} \times 50\text{ memos per day per typist} = 150\text{ memos per day}
\]

Therefore, three typists can type \boxed{150} memos in one day.
