What is the area of the figure, in square units? [asy]
draw((0,0)--(8,0)--(8,5)--(2,5)--(2,8)--(0,8)--cycle,linewidth(1));
draw((.5,0)--(.5,.5)--(0,.5),linewidth(1));
draw((7.5,0)--(7.5,.5)--(8,.5),linewidth(1));
draw((8,4.5)--(7.5,4.5)--(7.5,5),linewidth(1));
draw((0,7.5)--(.5,7.5)--(.5,8),linewidth(1));
draw((1.5,8)--(1.5,7.5)--(2,7.5),linewidth(1));
label("2",(1,8),N);
label("5",(8,2.5),E);
label("6",(5,5),N);
label("3",(2,6.5),E);
[/asy]

Solution:
answer:  To find the area of the figure, we need to calculate the area of the rectangle and subtract the areas of the two right triangles.

The area of the rectangle is $8 \times 5 = 40$ square units.

The area of one right triangle is $\frac{1}{2} \times 2 \times 3 = 3$ square units.

Since there are two right triangles, the total area of the triangles is $2 \times 3 = 6$ square units.

Therefore, the area of the figure is $40 - 6 = 34$ square units.
