The smallest positive integer greater than $1$ that is not divisible by any of the integers from $1$ to $20$ is $1$. However, the smallest positive integer greater than $1$ that is relatively prime to $20!$ is $1$ itself, because $1$ is relatively prime to every integer.

Thus, the smallest positive integer greater than $1$ that is relatively prime to $20!$ is $\boxed{1}$.
