answer:  The rectangular coordinates of the point with spherical coordinates $(\rho, -\theta, \phi)$ are the same as the rectangular coordinates of the point with spherical coordinates $(\rho, \theta, \phi)$ because the angle $\theta$ is unchanged when replaced by $-\theta$. Therefore, the rectangular coordinates of the point are $\boxed{(8, -3, -1)}$.
