Solution:
answer:  We know that the rectangular coordinates of a point with spherical coordinates $(\rho, \theta, \phi)$ are given by $(\rho \sin \phi, \rho \sin \phi, -\rho \cos \phi).$ Therefore, the rectangular coordinates of the point with spherical coordinates $(\rho, \theta, 2 \phi)$ are $(\rho \sin \phi, \rho \sin \phi, -\rho \cos \phi).$

