The cross product $\mathbf{c} \times \mathbf{a}$ is perpendicular to both $\mathbf{c}$ and $\mathbf{a},$ so the angle between $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{c}$ is $90^\circ.$

Therefore, the smallest possible angle between $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{c}$ is $\boxed{90^\circ}.$
