answer:  We have that $\mathbf{A}^3 = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & 7 \\ -1 & -2 \end{pmatrix},$ so $\mathbf{A}^{27} = (\mathbf{A}^3)^9 = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & 7 \\ -1 & -2 \end{pmatrix},$ $\mathbf{A}^{31} = (\mathbf{A}^3)^{10} \mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & 7 \\ -1 & -2 \end{pmatrix},$ and $\mathbf{A}^{40} = (\mathbf{A}^3)^{13} \mathbf{A}^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & 7 \\ -1 & -2 \end{pmatrix}.$ Therefore, $\mathbf{A}^{27} + \mathbf{A}^{31} + \mathbf{A}^{40} = \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 3 & 7 \\ -1 & -2 \end{pmatrix}}.$
