$$\tan{19x^{\circ}}=\tan{96^{\circ}}.$$

This implies that

$$19x^{\circ}=96^{\circ}+180^{\circ}k$$

for some integer $k$. Solving for $x$, we get

$$x=4^{\circ}+10^{\circ}k.$$

The smallest positive integer solution is $x=4^{\circ}$.

