answer:  We have that $\mathbf{v} \times \mathbf{b} = \mathbf{c} \times \mathbf{b}$ implies that $\mathbf{v}$ is orthogonal to both $\mathbf{b}$ and $\mathbf{c}$. Therefore, $\mathbf{v}$ must be orthogonal to $\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c} = \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}$.

